raLoaderModelOnly", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.5.2"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoraLoaderModelOnly"}, "order": 28}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "MODEL", "links": [312], "label": "模型", "type": "MODEL", "localized_name": "模型"}], "size": [640, 90], "pos": [-1870, 4680], "widgets_values": ["minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors", "default"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "unet_name"}, "name": "unet_name", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "UNET名称"}, {"widget": {"name": "weight_dtype"}, "name": "weight_dtype", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "剪枝类型"}], "flags": {}, "id": 127, "type": "UNETLoader", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "models": [{"directory_invalid": true, "name": "minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors", "directory": "diffusion_models", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors"}], "ver": "0.30.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.5.2"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "UNETLoader"}, "order": 7}, {"outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "links": [301], "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "字符串"}], "color": "#322", "widgets_values": ["subject_definitions\n\n<Subject 1> is the male model from <Picture 1>.\nUse <Picture 1> ONLY as a human identity and body reference.\nPreserve only the model's body proportions, neck structure, shoulders, arms, hands, skin tone, posture tendency, and overall mature male fashion-model presence.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe clothing visible in <Picture 1> is completely irrelevant and must be ignored.\nDo NOT inherit, preserve, blend, copy, transfer, or reference any clothing information from <Picture 1>, including but not limited to:\n- color\n- brightness\n- saturation\n- fabric texture\n- collar shape\n- neckline\n- sleeve length\n- garment silhouette\n- buttons\n- placket\n- folds\n- seam structure\n- style category\n- layering logic\n\n<Subject 2> is the target men's jacket defined ONLY by <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>.\n<Picture 2> is the ONLY authoritative source for the FRONT view of the jacket.\n<Picture 3> is the ONLY authoritative source for the BACK view of the jacket.\n\nAll garment-related information must come exclusively from <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>, including:\n- color family\n- hue\n- brightness\n- material appearance\n- silhouette\n- collar construction\n- zipper structure\n- pocket placement\n- sleeve pocket design\n- cuffs\n- hem\n- seams\n- proportions\n- internal visible structure if naturally exposed by the jacket\n\n<Picture 2> and <Picture 3> describe the same physical jacket.\nThe jacket must remain fully consistent during motion and body rotation.\n\nsummary\n\n[reference generation]\nCreate a premium 15-second vertical menswear product-commercial video in 9:16 format.\n\nThe male model from <Picture 1> is wearing the target jacket defined by <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>.\nThe purpose of the video is to clearly showcase the jacket on a real male model in a luxury hotel lobby / business-travel setting.\n\nThe video should feel like a refined menswear commercial:\nmature,\nmasculine,\npremium,\nbusiness casual,\nmodern urban lifestyle,\nhigh-end fashion advertising.\n\nThe video should focus on:\n1. a strong front-view introduction,\n2. elegant walking movement in a premium hotel space,\n3. clear collar / zipper / front-structure visibility,\n4. sleeve-pocket detail showcase,\n5. a natural body turn revealing the back,\n6. a final front-facing hero shot.\n\nretention_analysis\n\n<Subject 1> retention:\nPreserve the male model identity and human body traits from <Picture 1>, including:\n- body build\n- shoulder width\n- neck and jaw area proportions\n- arm shape\n- hand structure\n- skin tone\n- natural masculine presence\n\nDo NOT preserve the original upper-body clothing from <Picture 1> in any way.\n\nFULL GARMENT REPLACEMENT IS MANDATORY:\nThe original upper-body clothing visible in <Picture 1> must be completely removed and fully replaced by the target jacket from <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>.\n\nThis is NOT:\n- a recolor\n- a partial edit\n- a style transfer\n- a hybrid garment\n- a layering task\n\nThis IS:\n- a full clothing replacement task\n\nDo not preserve any part of the original shirt from <Picture 1>, including:\n- polo collar\n- neckline\n- placket\n- buttons\n- chest opening\n- sleeve edges\n- shirt color\n- inner shirt logic\n- any visible shirt remains\n\nNO ORIGINAL INNER SHIRT MAY REMAIN VISIBLE:\nDo not leave any visible remains of the original clothing from <Picture 1> at:\n- neck opening\n- chest opening\n- collar area\n- shoulder edge\n- sleeve opening\n- hem area\n\nDo not show a separate T-shirt, polo shirt, undershirt, or inner top unless it is explicitly supported by the garment references.\nIf the jacket is slightly open, the visible inner area must follow the jacket's authentic internal structure from <Picture 2>/<Picture 3>, not the original clothing from <Picture 1>.\n\n<Subject 2> retention:\nPreserve the jacket with very high product fidelity.\nThe jacket must match <Picture 2> for front-facing views and <Picture 3> for back-facing views.\n\nSTRICT SOURCE SEPARATION:\n<Picture 1> contributes ONLY the human model.\n<Picture 2>/<Picture 3> contribute ALL clothing information.\n\nCOLOR IS A HARD CONSTRAINT:\nThe final worn jacket must preserve the exact color direction, material feel, and visual logic of the jacket shown in <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>.\n\nUnder no circumstances may the model use, blend, sample, inherit, approximate, or transfer the clothing color from <Picture 1>.\n\nThe original green shirt color from <Picture 1> must NOT influence the jacket in any way.\nDo not tint the jacket toward green.\nDo not preserve the original shirt’s color logic.\nDo not mix the original shirt tone into the jacket body, collar, cuffs, sleeves, shadows, highlights, folds, or hem.\n\nIf any conflict exists between <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>/<Picture 3>, always discard all clothing information from <Picture 1> and strictly follow <Picture 2>/<Picture 3>.\n\nDo not invent extra garment elements.\nDo not hallucinate:\n- extra logos\n- extra text\n- extra pockets\n- extra straps\n- extra zippers\n- new decorations\n- new patches\n- new layers\n- unsupported inner garments\n\nNegative constraints:\n- do not keep the original polo-shirt color\n- do not keep the original polo-shirt collar\n- do not preserve the original neckline from <Picture 1>\n- do not create a hybrid between the original shirt and the target jacket\n- do not create layered clothing unless clearly supported by the jacket references\n- do not reveal an inner T-shirt or polo\n- do not mix the original shirt into the jacket\n- do not reinterpret the jacket into another color palette\n- do not generate a jacket that still feels like the shirt from <Picture 1>\n\ndetailed_description\n\n[Shot 1 | 0.0s - 2.0s]\nA premium medium waist-up shot inside an upscale modern hotel lobby.\n<Subject 1> is already fully wearing <Subject 2>.\nThe original clothing from <Picture 1> must be completely absent.\nThe jacket front must strictly follow <Picture 2>.\nNo visible polo collar, no undershirt neckline, no original shirt remains.\nThe model stands calmly near a large floor-to-ceiling window or elegant stone wall.\nWarm architectural indoor light combines with soft natural window light.\nThe camera performs a slow elegant push-in.\nThe jacket is the primary visual focus.\n\n[Shot 2 | 2.0s - 4.2s]\nThe model begins walking slowly and naturally through the luxury hotel lobby.\nUse a medium shot with smooth side tracking.\nThe movement is restrained, confident, and premium.\nClearly show the front silhouette of the jacket while walking.\nThe jacket front must remain faithful to <Picture 2>.\nNatural walking motion should create realistic folds in the body and sleeves.\nDo not reveal any original clothing from <Picture 1>.\n\n[Shot 3 | 4.2s - 6.3s]\nA closer chest-level tracking shot.\nFocus on the collar construction, zipper area, upper chest structure, and fabric surface.\nThe model continues a very gentle slow walk or a subtle pause.\nShow the jacket’s materials and stitching clearly.\nAll visible front-side details must strictly follow <Picture 2>.\nNo green tint.\nNo shirt neckline.\nNo hybrid layering.\n\n[Shot 4 | 6.3s - 8.5s]\nA controlled product detail close-up of the sleeve and utility-pocket area.\nThe model makes one small natural arm movement, such as slightly lifting the forearm or adjusting posture.\nShow the sleeve pocket structure, zipper, stitching, seam behavior, and fabric volume clearly.\nUse shallow depth of field.\nThe hotel environment stays softly blurred.\nDo not invent extra hardware or design changes.\n\n[Shot 5 | 8.5s - 10.8s]\nReturn to a medium shot near a refined hotel passage or window area.\nThe model stops walking and slowly rotates his torso and upper body from the front toward the side and then toward the back.\nThis is one continuous, smooth, natural turn.\nThe jacket must remain consistent during the transition.\nFront-facing clothing information follows <Picture 2>, and rear-facing clothing information gradually transitions toward <Picture 3>.\nDo not allow the original clothing from <Picture 1> to reappear during motion.\n\n[Shot 6 | 10.8s - 12.8s]\nThe model now clearly presents the back of the jacket.\nThe back must accurately follow <Picture 3>.\nShow the rear collar, shoulder structure, back panel, sleeve silhouette, hem, and overall back proportions clearly.\nUse a slight lateral camera move or a very subtle follow movement.\nWarm hotel lighting outlines the garment silhouette.\nKeep the shot elegant and restrained.\n\n[Shot 7 | 12.8s - 15.0s]\nThe model smoothly turns back into a three-quarter front hero pose.\nThe front appearance must return strictly to <Picture 2>.\nHe performs one subtle premium menswear gesture, such as lightly adjusting the collar or touching the front edge of the jacket.\nDo not perform multiple gestures at once.\nNo original shirt may appear.\nEnd on a stable waist-up hero shot.\nThe final frame should clearly showcase the jacket silhouette, collar, front structure, sleeves, and overall masculine fit.\n\noverall_visual_direction\n\nPremium luxury hotel menswear campaign.\nModern business travel lifestyle.\nMature masculine aesthetic.\nHigh-end commercial photography.\nWarm architectural lighting.\nSoft natural window light.\nSubtle cinematic contrast.\nPolished stone.\nDark wood.\nBrushed metal.\nMinimal luxury interiors.\nRealistic skin.\nRealistic fabric.\nNatural clothing folds.\nShallow depth of field.\nRestrained camera movement.\nClean composition.\n\nThe environment must support the garment and never overpower it.\nThe jacket must always remain the visual priority.\n\ncamera_language\n\nUse mostly medium shots, waist-up shots, chest-level close-ups, and garment detail close-ups.\nUse slow dolly movement, smooth side tracking, subtle arc tracking during rotation, and precise detail close-ups.\nNo handheld shake.\nNo fast camera movement.\nNo rapid zooms.\nNo unstable motion.\nNo exaggerated slow motion.\nAvoid wide shots unless the jacket remains clearly visible.\n\noverall_soundscape\n\nQuiet premium hotel ambience.\nSubtle indoor space tone, faint distant environmental presence, and gentle fabric rustling when the model walks, turns, or lightly adjusts the jacket.\nNo dialogue.\nNo narration.\nNo loud transition effects.\n\nnon_diegetic_music\n\nA premium modern menswear commercial instrumental.\nTempo around 95-105 BPM.\nMinimal deep percussion.\nSubtle bass.\nRefined modern electronic texture.\nSophisticated, understated, masculine, and contemporary.\nNo vocals.\nThe music should support the clean pacing of the fashion showcase, build slightly during the walking and rotation section, and resolve calmly during the final hero shot.\n\nFINAL HARD RULES:\n\nThis is a full clothing replacement task.\nThe model from <Picture 1> must wear ONLY the jacket defined by <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>.\n\nThe original upper-body clothing from <Picture 1> must be completely removed and must never remain visible.\n\nDo not show:\n- the original polo collar\n- any undershirt neckline\n- any original shirt opening\n- any original garment color influence\n- any layered-shirt effect\n\nOnly the target jacket may appear as the visible upper-body garment.\n\nIf ambiguity occurs, prioritize garment fidelity over stylistic creativity.\nIf ambiguity occurs, discard all clothing information from <Picture 1>."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "值"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Input Text (Prompt)", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#533", "size": [590, 1140], "pos": [1020, 5660], "id": 138, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.5.2"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 8}, {"showAdvanced": false, "outputs": [{"name": "width", "links": [276], "label": "width", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "width"}, {"name": "height", "links": [277], "label": "height", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "height"}], "color": "#322", "widgets_values": ["16:9 (Widescreen)", 0.7, 32], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "aspect_ratio"}, "name": "aspect_ratio", "label": "aspect_ratio", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "aspect_ratio"}, {"widget": {"name": "megapixels"}, "name": "megapixels", "label": "megapixels", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "megapixels"}, {"widget": {"name": "multiple"}, "name": "multiple", "label": "multiple", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "multip